<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Strength</h1>
<p>Strength (STR) is one of your abilities: how strong you are. It 
determines:
</p>
<ul><li>How well you fight with most weapons. Each weapon draws on two of your abilities: nearly all, swords, axes, clubs, maces and even daggers, on two parts strength to one part dexterity; only the whip, the sickle and the bow, crossbow and sling lean on dexterity instead (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>).</li>
<li>How much weight you can carry: 50, plus half your own weight (at least 50), plus twice your strength.</li>
<li>How well you move in armour. Heavy armour slows you down in a fight; strength, and practice in that kind of armour, make up for it, the more so the heavier the armour (see <a cmd='#'>Help Armor</a>).</li></ul>
<p>The spell strength raises it for a while (see <a cmd='#'>Help Spell Strength</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
